# ============================================================
# Netlify redirects — https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/
#
# Legacy WordPress URLs. The old WP Engine site served the legal
# pages at these paths; these 301s keep the old links (and their
# search ranking) working now that wifisquared.com is on Netlify.
#
# Verified live on the WP site 20260729:
#   /privacy-policy/                        -> the privacy policy
#   /terms-of-service/                      -> 301s to the line below
#   /terms-of-service-and-return-policy/    -> the terms page
#
# Targets are the extensionless URLs, not privacy.html/terms.html.
# Netlify serves both forms 200 (verified 20260731), and the site's
# own footers link to the extensionless pair — so pointing the 301s
# there lands the old links on the same URL everything else cites
# instead of splitting the ranking across two spellings.
# ============================================================

/privacy-policy                       /privacy   301
/terms-of-service-and-return-policy   /terms     301
/terms-of-service                     /terms     301

# internal/ holds working drafts — the FCC label data, the label generator,
# and the superseded network management disclosure. It is excluded from the
# deploy bundle rather than published and blocked, so this rule is a backstop
# for the day someone deploys the repo root as-is. An unreviewed policy draft
# reachable by URL is a liability even when nothing links to it.
#
# The trailing ! is load-bearing. Without it an existing file shadows the rule
# and Netlify serves the file instead of the redirect — verified: these paths
# returned 200 until the force flag was added.
/internal/*                           /404.html  404!
